<.shell current={:phone}>
  <h1>Phone</h1>
  <p class="lead">A phone number with a copy button, and Call and Text buttons.</p>

  <div class="demo max-w-sm">
    <dl>
      <dt>Phone</dt>
      <dd>
        <.phone
          id="phone-demo"
          phone="6045551234"
          call_and_text
          touch_only={false}
          class="mt-2"
        />
      </dd>
      <dt>Emergency contact</dt>
      <dd>
        Robin Park (Partner)<br />
        <.phone id="phone-demo-contact" phone="604-555-0100" />
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    Any phone number people use to reach someone: a member's details, an emergency contact, yet to arrive, and no-shows. Add Call and Text where someone may want to reach them now.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    Your own number, such as on Your membership: there's no one to reach. Show it with <code>Service.Phone.format/1</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.phone id="…" phone=&#123;member.phone&#125; /&gt;</code>
    shows the number as <code>Service.Phone.format/1</code>
    writes it, then a copy button. Add <code>call_and_text</code>
    for Call and Text buttons under it. They show only on a touch screen, because a desktop often has no app for
    <code>tel:</code>
    and <code>sms:</code>
    links. The example above shows them everywhere with <code>touch_only=&#123;false&#125;</code>. With no number it shows nothing, or the hint in <code>missing</code>, such as "No mobile number".
  </p>
</.shell>
